From: SP11 audio reverse-engineering project
Date: 2026-07-26
Subject: [INSTRUMENTATION PATCH] soundwire: qcom: log static port allocation

Add dynamic-debug output for each slave-to-master port mapping accepted by
the Qualcomm SoundWire allocator.  Mark a mapping as reused when its master
port was already present in the controller port mask.

This temporary observation-only patch is intended to establish the actual
SP11 playback stream layout, particularly the two amplifiers' shared PBR
master port 7 and distinct VISENSE master ports 10 and 11.  It does not
change allocation or hardware-programming behaviour and emits no messages
unless dynamic debug is enabled for this call site.

---
 drivers/soundwire/qcom.c | 9 +++++++++
 1 file changed, 9 insertions(+)

diff --git a/drivers/soundwire/qcom.c b/drivers/soundwire/qcom.c
index 3d8f5a81eff1..35eb4f63aacc 100644
--- a/drivers/soundwire/qcom.c
+++ b/drivers/soundwire/qcom.c
@@ -1230,6 +1230,7 @@ static int qcom_swrm_stream_alloc_ports(struct qcom_swrm_ctrl *ctrl,
 	unsigned long *port_mask;
 	int maxport, pn, nports = 0;
 	unsigned int m_port;
+	bool port_in_use;
 	struct sdw_port_config *pconfig __free(kfree) = kzalloc_objs(*pconfig,
 								     ctrl->nports);
 	if (!pconfig)
@@ -1275,6 +1276,14 @@ static int qcom_swrm_stream_alloc_ports(struct qcom_swrm_ctrl *ctrl,
 					dev_err(ctrl->dev, "All ports busy\n");
 					return -EBUSY;
 				}
+
+				port_in_use = test_bit(pn, port_mask);
+				dev_dbg(ctrl->dev,
+					"stream=%s bus=%d dev=%u sport=%u mport=%d mask=%#x%s\n",
+					stream->name, ctrl->bus.id, slave->dev_num,
+					p_rt->num, pn, p_rt->ch_mask,
+					port_in_use ? " reused" : "");
+
 				set_bit(pn, port_mask);
 				pconfig[nports].num = pn;
 				pconfig[nports].ch_mask = p_rt->ch_mask;
-- 
